#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:27
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:29
msgid ""
"This document contains the release notes for the Clang C/C++/Objective-C "
"frontend, part of the LLVM Compiler Infrastructure, release {{env.config."
"release}}. Here we describe the status of Clang in some detail, including "
"major improvements from the previous release and new feature work. For the "
"general LLVM release notes, see [the LLVM documentation](https://llvm.org/"
"docs/ReleaseNotes.html). For the libc++ release notes, see [this page]"
"(https://libcxx.llvm.org/ReleaseNotes.html). All LLVM releases may be "
"downloaded from the [LLVM releases web site](https://llvm.org/releases/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:38
msgid ""
"For more information about Clang or LLVM, including information about the "
"latest release, please see the [Clang Web Site](https://clang.llvm.org) or "
"the [LLVM Web Site](https://llvm.org)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:42
msgid "Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:44
msgid "C/C++ Language Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:46
msgid ""
"`-Wunicode-whitespace` now defaults to an error. The previous behavior can "
"be restored with `-Wno-error=unicode-whitespace`. Clang will stop accepting "
"non-ascii whitespaces as token separators in a future version of Clang."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:51
msgid "C++ Specific Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:53
msgid ""
"The `[[carries_dependency]]` attribute is no longer recognized, in any "
"language mode, as it was removed from the standard by [P3475R2](https://wg21."
"link/P3475R2)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:58
msgid "Objective-C Specific Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:60
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where AST consumers based on `RecursiveASTVisitor` would "
"bypass the exception parameter declaration inside Objective-C `@catch` "
"blocks. This could cause tooling that previously ignored the parameter "
"declaration to now find valid issues. (#GH212564)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:65
msgid "ABI Changes in This Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:67
msgid ""
"Except on PlayStation, Clang now derives the x86-64 System V AVX ABI level "
"for 256- and 512-bit vector arguments and returns from effective per-"
"function target features. Features and `arch=` CPUs that imply AVX or "
"AVX512F are honored, and calls use the caller's features, matching GCC. Per-"
"function features cannot lower the translation-unit ABI level; `-fclang-abi-"
"compat=23` restores the previous behavior. (#GH193298)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:74
msgid ""
"On SPARC, a `_Complex` value with an integer element type is now passed and "
"returned packed into the one or two integer registers it fits in, matching "
"GCC. Clang previously passed such a value indirectly and returned it with "
"one part per register. `-fclang-abi-compat=23` restores the previous "
"behavior. (#GH212340)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:80
msgid ""
"On SPARC64, a `_Complex char` or `_Complex short` is now right-justified in "
"its slot in the parameter array, like every other scalar narrower than a "
"slot, rather than left-justified the way a small struct is. `-fclang-abi-"
"compat=23` restores the previous behavior. (#GH212340)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:85
msgid ""
"On MIPS, a `_Complex` value with an integer element type is now returned "
"packed into a single integer register when it fits in one, matching GCC. A "
"`_Complex char` or `_Complex short`, and on N32/N64 also a `_Complex int`, "
"is no longer returned with one part per register. `-fclang-abi-compat=23` "
"restores the previous behavior. (#GH212109)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:91
msgid ""
"On MIPS N32/N64, a `_Complex float` or `_Complex double` argument is now "
"packed into integer registers, or onto the stack, once there is no longer "
"room to give each of its parts a floating-point register, matching GCC. "
"Clang previously always passed the parts separately. `-fclang-abi-compat=23` "
"restores the previous behavior. (#GH212109)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:97
msgid ""
"On MIPS N32/N64, an `__int128` now correctly start in an even-numbered "
"register or 16-byte aligned stack slot, matching GCC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:100
msgid ""
"Except on PlayStation, on x86-64 System V a non-zero-width unnamed bit-field "
"now classifies the eightbytes it occupies as INTEGER, like a named bit-"
"field, matching GCC. Aggregates where this changes the classification may be "
"passed or returned differently -- a struct holding a run of `__int128` bit-"
"fields, for example, now travels in the two integer registers the ABI "
"assigns it. This also fixes a crash when such a struct was passed or "
"returned. `-fclang-abi-compat=23` restores the previous behavior. (#GH202205)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:108
msgid ""
"On 32-bit x86, Clang now matches GCC when classifying arguments for the "
"`regparm` calling convention. Floating-point types other than `float` and "
"`double` no longer consume general-purpose register slots, complex values "
"are passed on the stack without consuming register slots, and unions are no "
"longer classified according to a single member. `-fclang-abi-compat=23` "
"restores the previous behavior. (#GH227130)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:115
msgid ""
"Clang now considers matrix types in its isHomogeneousAggregate() handling, "
"which can lead to differences in how structures containing matrix types are "
"classified for ABI purposes. The previous exclusion of matrix types appears "
"to have been accidental. Matrix types now follow the same rules as arrays "
"for homogeneous aggregate classification. `-fclang-abi-compat=23` restores "
"the previous behavior. (#GH218799)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:122
msgid "AST Dumping Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:124
msgid "Clang Frontend Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:126
msgid "Templight support has been removed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:128
msgid ""
"`-fstack-clash-protection` has been enabled implicitly by default for "
"android target triples (except 32b arm targets). Can be disabled via `-fno-"
"stack-clash-protection`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:132
msgid "Clang Python Bindings Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:134
msgid ""
"`CompletionChunkKind` instance's `__str__` representation has been adapted "
"to be consistent with other enums in the library. The representation now "
"follows the `CompletionChunkKind.VARIANT_NAME` scheme instead of "
"`VariantName`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:137
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated `SPELLING_CACHE` alias. All usage should be migrated "
"to use `CompletionChunk.SPELLING_CACHE` instead. Note that this uses "
"`CompletionChunkKind` enumeration as keys, instead of integer values."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:141
msgid ""
"Remove the deprecated `CompletionChunk.isKind...` methods. Existing uses "
"should be adapted to directly compare equality of the `CompletionChunk` kind "
"with the corresponding `CompletionChunkKind` variant."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:144
msgid ""
"Affected methods: `isKindOptional`, `isKindTypedText`, `isKindPlaceHolder`, "
"`isKindInformative` and `isKindResultType`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:147
msgid ""
"`CompletionString.availability` now returns instances of `AvailabilityKind`. "
"As a result, the `__str__` representation of its return values changed. Like "
"other libclang enums, it now follows the `CompletionChunkKind.VARIANT_NAME` "
"scheme instead of `VariantName`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:151
msgid ""
"`Cursor` instance's `enum_value` method now returns 1 instead of -1 for "
"`true` bool enumeration values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:153
msgid "OpenCL Potentially Breaking Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:155
msgid "What's New in Clang {{env.config.release}}?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:157
msgid "C++ Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:158
msgid ""
"Clang now supports friend declarations with a dependent nested name "
"specifier. (#GH104057)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:160
msgid "``auto()`` casts are accepted as an extension pre-C++23."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:162
msgid "C++2d Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:164
msgid ""
"Clang now supports [P3658R1](https://wg21.link/p3658r1) (Adjust identifier "
"following new Unicode recommendations), applied as a DR to all C++ language "
"modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:168
msgid ""
"Clang now supports [P3670R4](https://wg21.link/p3670r4) (Pack indexing for "
"template names), which allows a pack of templates to be indexed, as in `TT..."
"[0]<int>`. Like pack indexing of types and expressions, this is available in "
"all C++ language modes as an extension, controlled by `-Wc++2d-extensions` "
"and `-Wpre-c++2d-compat`, and `__cpp_pack_indexing` is bumped to `202606L`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:175
msgid "C++2c Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:177
msgid ""
"Added `__builtin_type_order` for compatibility with GCC as part of the "
"implementation of [P2830R10](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/"
"papers/2025/p2830r10.html) (Constexpr Type Ordering)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:180
msgid ""
"Clang now supports [P3533R2](https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg21/docs/"
"papers/2025/p3533r2.html) (constexpr virtual inheritance)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:182
msgid ""
"Implemented the language part of [P3475R2](https://wg21.link/P3475R2) "
"(Defang and deprecate `memory_order::consume`) by removing support for the "
"`[[carries_dependency]]` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:186
msgid "C++23 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:188
msgid "C++20 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:190
msgid ""
"Now clang-scan-deps in P1689 format can find the dependencies described in "
"module map file. See the documents of standard C++ modules for details."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:193
msgid "C++17 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:195
msgid "Resolutions to C++ Defect Reports"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:197
msgid ""
"Clang now falls back to alignment-aware allocation functions for non-"
"overaligned types, implementing [CWG2282](https://wg21.link/cwg2282)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:200
msgid ""
"Clang now converts floating-point values to boolean first when converting "
"them to an enumeration type with a fixed `bool` underlying type. This "
"resolves [CWG1094](https://wg21.link/cwg1094)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:204
msgid "C Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:206
msgid "C2y Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:208
msgid ""
"Clang now supports C2y's new syntax for `if` and `switch` statements with "
"initializer and condition variables, as specified in [N3356](https://www."
"open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n3356.htm)_. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:233
msgid ""
"Clang now diagnoses the use of the same identifier with both internal and "
"external linkage within a translation unit, as made ill-formed by [N3410]"
"(https://www.open-std.org/jtc1/sc22/wg14/www/docs/n3410.pdf). This is also "
"diagnosed in older C language modes as the behavior was undefined prior to "
"C2y. (#GH54215)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:239
msgid "C23 Feature Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:241
msgid "Objective-C Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:243
msgid "Non-comprehensive list of changes in this release"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:245
msgid ""
"Clang tools now resolve tool names without a path in compilation databases "
"through `PATH`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:248
msgid ""
"On musl targets, the driver now links ``libssp_nonshared.a`` when stack "
"protection is enabled and the library is present in the toolchain library "
"paths, matching what musl distributions configure GCC to do."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:252
msgid ""
"Clang now allows GNU computed `goto` extension in `constexpr` functions, "
"matching the relaxed `constexpr` function body rules introduced in C++23."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:255
msgid ""
"Added support for the `__builtin_strlcat` and `__builtin_strlcpy` builtins."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:257
msgid ""
"Added `__builtin_sort_pack` to sort a pack of types using the same order as "
"`__builtin_type_order`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:260
msgid "New Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:262
msgid ""
"New option `-fdefined-pointer-subtraction` added to preserve stable "
"semantics when subtracting pointers to unrelated objects."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:265
msgid ""
"Added `--print-cxx-stdlib` and `--print-cxx-stdlib-include-dirs` to print "
"the C++ standard library selected by the driver and the include directories "
"added for it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:269
msgid ""
"Added `-mscs-reg=<reg>` on Hexagon to select which callee-saved register "
"(`r16`-`r27`, default `r18`) holds the shadow call stack pointer under `-"
"fsanitize=shadow-call-stack`. The selected register must also be reserved "
"with the matching `-ffixed-<reg>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:274
msgid ""
"Added `-fmodules-ignore-search-path=<path>`, the search-path counterpart to "
"`-fmodules-ignore-macro=<macro>`: the path is dropped from the context hash "
"of every module and physically removed from every module build, and kept "
"only for the translation unit itself. This lets builds that differ only in a "
"search path share one module cache, and is only sound when no module needs "
"the path -- a lookup that would have resolved through an ignored path simply "
"fails."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:281
msgid ""
"Added support for `-fkeep-inline-functions` in Clang. This option forces "
"inline function definitions that are available in the current translation "
"unit to be emitted into the object file, even when they are inlined into all "
"callers or are otherwise unused."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:286
msgid "Deprecated Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:288
msgid "Modified Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:290
msgid ""
"All options of the `-fzero-call-used-regs` compiler flag are now allowed on "
"RISC-V."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:292
msgid ""
"`-ftrivial-auto-var-init=` now initializes variables whose declaration is "
"bypassed by a `goto` or `switch`, which were previously left uninitialized. "
"The initialization is emitted at each bypassing jump. See the `-ftrivial-"
"auto-var-init=` entry in the User's Manual for the details, including where "
"C deliberately departs from C 6.2.4p6."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:298
msgid "Removed Compiler Flags"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:300
msgid "Attribute Changes in Clang"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:302
msgid ""
"Clang now properly propagates attributes on class and variable templates to "
"their redeclarations, which will result in redeclarations not interfering "
"with diagnostics. (#GH209812)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:304
msgid ""
"Clang now recognizes the `[[gnu::flag_enum]]` attribute and treats it "
"equivalent to `[[clang::flag_enum]]`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:306
msgid ""
"Clang now accepts `_single_inheritance` under `-fms-compatibility` as an "
"alias for `__single_inheritance`; `_multiple_inheritance` and "
"`_virtual_inheritance` were already correctly supported as aliases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:308
msgid "Improvements to Clang's diagnostics"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:310
msgid ""
"`-Wfortify-source` now diagnoses when `strlcat`, `__builtin_strlcat`, "
"`strlcpy`, or `__builtin_strlcpy` is called with a size argument larger than "
"the destination buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:313
msgid ""
"`-Wfortify-source` now diagnoses when `recv` or `recvfrom` is called with a "
"size argument larger than the destination buffer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:316
msgid ""
"`-Wfortify-source` now diagnoses when `poll`, `ppoll`, or `ppoll64` is "
"called with a descriptor count whose total size exceeds the `fds` array size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:319
msgid ""
"The `cannot overload a member function` diagnostic now describes the "
"previous declaration first, matching the order in which the declarations "
"appear in the source. (#GH219803)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:323
msgid "More consistent rendering of Unicode characters in diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:325
msgid ""
"Fixed `-Wunused-parameter` to diagnose coroutine parameters that are only "
"considered during allocation function lookup or promise object "
"initialization, while not diagnosing parameters passed to the selected "
"allocation function or promise constructor. (#GH217501)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:330
msgid ""
"The `wb` and `uwb` `_BitInt` literal suffixes are no longer diagnosed by "
"default before C23. They stay in `-Wc23-extensions` and are still reported "
"under `-pedantic` or when that group is enabled explicitly, matching how the "
"`_BitInt` type itself is already handled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:335
msgid ""
"Fixed bug in `-Wdocumentation` so that it correctly handles explicit "
"function template instantiations (#64087)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:338
msgid ""
"When a `constexpr` range-based for loop variable cannot be initialized by a "
"constant expression, Clang now emits a single note identifying the read of "
"the loop's implicit `__begin` variable, instead of a generic note about "
"reading a non-constexpr variable followed by a `declared here` note. "
"(#GH211926)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:344
msgid ""
"Fixed concept template parameters not being recognized in `-Wdocumentation` "
"when mentioned in tparam comments. (#GH64087)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:347
msgid ""
"`-Wunused-but-set-variable` now diagnoses file-scope variables with internal "
"linkage (`static` storage class) that are assigned but never used. This new "
"coverage is added under the subgroup `-Wunused-but-set-global`, allowing it "
"to be disabled independently with `-Wno-unused-but-set-global`. (#GH148361)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:353
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety` to enable lifetime safety analysis, a CFG-based "
"intra-procedural analysis that detects use-after-free and related temporal "
"safety bugs. See the [RFC](https://discourse.llvm.org/t/rfc-intra-procedural-"
"lifetime-analysis-in-clang/86291) for more details. By design, this warning "
"is enabled in `-Weverything`. To disable the analysis, use `-Wno-lifetime-"
"safety` or `-fno-lifetime-safety`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:360
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety-suggestions` to enable lifetime annotation "
"suggestions. This provides suggestions for function parameters that should "
"be marked `[[clang::lifetimebound]]` based on lifetime analysis. For "
"example, for the following function:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:369
msgid "Clang will suggest:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:381
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety-noescape` to detect misuse of `[[clang::noescape]]` "
"annotation where the parameter escapes through return. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:388
msgid "Clang will warn:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:399
msgid ""
"Added `-Wlifetime-safety-dangling-field` to detect dangling field references "
"when stack memory escapes to class fields. This is part of `-Wlifetime-"
"safety` and detects cases where local variables or parameters are stored in "
"fields but outlive their scope. For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:411
msgid ""
"Lifetime safety analysis is now enabled for C by default. The `-"
"fexperimental-lifetime-safety-c` flag is renamed to `-flifetime-safety-c`. "
"Use `-fno-lifetime-safety-c` to disable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:414
msgid ""
"Improved `-Wassign-enum` performance by caching enum enumerator values. "
"(#GH176454)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:416
msgid ""
"Fixed a false negative in `-Warray-bounds` where the warning was suppressed "
"when accessing a member function on a past-the-end array element. (#GH179128)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:420
msgid ""
"Added a missing space to the FixIt for the `implicit-int` group of "
"diagnostics and made sure that only one such diagnostic and FixIt is emitted "
"per declaration group. (#GH179354)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:423
msgid ""
"Fixed the Fix-It insertion point for `expected ';' after alias declaration` "
"when parsing alias declarations involving a token-split `>>` sequence (for "
"example, `using A = X<int>>;`). (#GH184425)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:427
msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect `implicitly deleted` diagnostic for explicitly deleted "
"candidate function. (#GH185693)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:430
msgid ""
"The `-Wloop-analysis` warning has been extended to catch more cases of "
"variable modification inside lambda expressions (#GH132038)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:433
msgid ""
"Clang now emits `-Wsizeof-pointer-memaccess` when snprintf/vsnprintf use the "
"sizeof the destination buffer(dynamically allocated) in the len "
"parameter(#GH162366)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:436
msgid ""
"Added `-Wmodule-map-path-outside-directory` (off by default) to warn on "
"header and umbrella directory paths that use `..` to refer outside the "
"module directory in module maps found via implicit search (`-fimplicit-"
"module-maps`). This does not affect module maps specified explicitly via `-"
"fmodule-map-file=`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:442
msgid ""
"Honour `[[maybe_unused]]` attribute on private fields. `-Wunused-private-"
"field` no longer emits a warning for annotated private fields."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:446
msgid ""
"Improved `-Wgnu-zero-variadic-macro-arguments` to suggest using `__VA_OPT__` "
"if the current language version supports it(#GH188624)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:449
msgid ""
"Clang now emits an error when implicitly casting a complex type to a built-"
"in vector type. (#GH186805)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:451
msgid ""
"Added `-Wnonportable-include-path-separator` (off by default) to catch "
"#include directives that use backslashes as a path separator. The warning "
"includes a FixIt to change all the backslashes to forward slashes, so that "
"the code can automatically be made portable to other host platforms that "
"don't support backslashes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:457
msgid ""
"Clang now explains why template deduction fails for explicit template "
"arguments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:459
msgid ""
"No longer emitting a `-Wpre-c2y-compat` or extension diagnostic about use of "
"octal literals with a `0o` prefix, and no longer emitting a `-Wdeprecated-"
"octal-literals` diagnostic for use of octal literals without a `0o` prefix, "
"when the literal is expanded from a macro defined in a system header. "
"(#GH192389)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:465
msgid ""
"Improved error recovery for missing semicolons after class members. Clang "
"now avoids skipping subsequent valid declarations when their previous decl "
"is missing semicolon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:468
msgid "Removed the body of lambdas from some diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:470
msgid ""
"Fixed false positive host-device mismatch errors in discarded `if constexpr` "
"branches for CUDA/HIP; such calls are now correctly skipped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:473
msgid ""
"Clang now errors when a function declaration aliases a variable or vice "
"versa. (#GH195550)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:475
msgid ""
"Added `-Wattribute-alias` to diagnose type mismatches between an alias and "
"its aliased function. (#GH195550)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:477
msgid ""
"The diagnostics around `__block` now explain why a variable cannot be marked "
"`__block`. (#GH197213)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:479
msgid ""
"Extended `-Wnonportable-include-path` to warn about trailing whitespace and "
"dots in `#include` paths. (#GH190610)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:481
msgid ""
"Clang now emits error when attribute is missing closing `]]` followed by `;;"
"`. (#GH187223)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:483
msgid ""
"Clang now rejects inline asm constraints and clobbers that contain an "
"embedded null character, instead of silently truncating them. (#GH173900)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:486
msgid ""
"Added `-Wstringop-overread` to warn when `memcpy`, `memmove`, `memcmp`, and "
"related builtins read more bytes than the source buffer size (#GH83728)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:489
msgid ""
"Diagnostics for the C++11 range-based for statement now report the correct "
"iterator type in notes for invalid iterator types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:492
msgid ""
"`-Wfortify-source` now diagnoses calls to `fread`, `fwrite`, and `fgets` "
"when the requested size exceeds the corresponding buffer. (#GH204337)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:495
msgid ""
"`-Wfortify-source` now warns when the constant-evaluated argument to `umask` "
"has bits set outside `0777`. Those bits are silently discarded by the "
"kernel, so setting them is almost always a typo (matching the bionic libc "
"`diagnose_if` check)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:500
msgid "Improved how Unicode characters are displayed in diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:502
msgid ""
"Clang no longer retains source comments in the AST when nothing will read "
"them back. Comments are now collected only when they may be consumed (e.g. "
"with ``-fparse-all-comments``, when ``-Wdocumentation`` is enabled, when "
"emitting a PCH/module, or during code completion), reducing memory overhead "
"for typical compilations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:508
msgid ""
"`-Wtautological-pointer-compare` and `-Wpointer-bool-conversion` now "
"diagnose a reference to a function (e.g. of type `void (&)()`) compared "
"against or converted to a null pointer, the same as a bare function name. "
"(#GH46362)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:513
msgid ""
"Clang now attempts to print enumerator names rather than C-style cast "
"expressions in more diagnostics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:516
msgid ""
"`-Wunsafe-buffer-usage` now warns about unsafe two-parameter constructors of "
"`std::string_view` (pointer and size), consistent with the existing warning "
"for `std::span`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:519
msgid ""
"`-Wno-unsafe-buffer-usage-in-static-sized-array` now also suppresses "
"warnings for pointer arithmetic on statically-sized arrays when the offset "
"is a non-negative constant within the array bounds."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:523
msgid ""
"`-Wc++98-compat` now diagnoses explicit conversion functions in C++20 and "
"later, matching the behavior in C++11 through C++17. (#GH161689)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:526
msgid ""
"Added `-Wcounter-extension` as a diagnostic group under `-Wc2y-extensions` "
"to control `__COUNTER__` being diagnosed as an extension. This allows `-"
"pedantic` users to disable the diagnostic with `-Wno-counter-extension` "
"without having to disable all pedantic diagnostics. (#GH196557)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:531
msgid "Clang now diagnoses more details when a constraint evaluates to false."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:533
msgid ""
"`-Wpointer-arith` no longer reports subtraction of pointers to a variably "
"modified type, such as `int[n]`, as a subtraction of pointers to a type of "
"zero size, unless the size is provably zero: a zero-sized base element or a "
"dimension that is a zero integer constant, as in `struct Empty vla[n]` or "
"`int vla[n][0]`. (#GH28328)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:539
msgid ""
"Fixed a missing `-Wconstant-conversion` diagnostic for signed `char` arrays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:541
msgid ""
"Clang now diagnoses passing wrong vector type as a mask to "
"`__builtin_shufflevector`. (#GH218132)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:543
msgid ""
"`-Wdelete-abstract-non-virtual-dtor` and `-Wdelete-non-abstract-non-virtual-"
"dtor` no longer warn when the selected deallocation function is a destroying "
"`operator delete`, since such a delete expression never invokes the "
"destructor. (#GH65524)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:548
msgid ""
"Fixed a false-positive `-Wshadow` warning when a variable in an inline-"
"defined friend function shares the name of a non-static class member "
"variable. (#GH221190)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:552
msgid ""
"Clang now diagnoses matrix logical operations are only supported for HLSL. "
"(#GH222381)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:554
msgid ""
"Improve the input size mismatch diagnostic when calling "
"`__builtin_shufflevector` with valid vector element types but different "
"sizes. (#GH221791)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:557
msgid ""
"Suggests the correct location for an attribute written before the `using` "
"keyword of an alias-declaration. (#GH155787)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:560
msgid ""
"Improve Clang diagnoses when unary `__imag` operator with non-complex type "
"operand is used as lvalue. (#GH222383)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:562
msgid "Improvements to Clang's time-trace"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:564
msgid "Improvements to Coverage Mapping"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:566
msgid "Bug Fixes in This Version"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:568
msgid ""
"Fixed incorrect handling of C++ import preprocessing token when a digraph "
"character after import. (#GH190693)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:569
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when emitting RTTI for a `dllexport` class, or the fundamental "
"type descriptors for `__cxxabiv1::__fundamental_type_info`, under `-"
"fvisibility=hidden`. (#GH207963)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:570
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when passing a wide string literal to "
"`__builtin_nan`. (#GH212108)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:571
msgid "Fixed a constraint comparison bug in partial ordering. (#GH182671)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:572
msgid ""
"Fixed a rejected-valid case that used an explicit object parameter in an out-"
"of-line definition of a nested class member. (#GH136472)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:573
msgid "Fixed an assertion on omp taskloop transparent (#GH197162)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:574
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where `__func__`, `__PRETTY_FUNCTION__` and `__FUNCTION__` were "
"not resolving to the proper function when inside a lambda return type "
"(#GH211811)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:575
msgid ""
"Fixed USR generation for declarations whose signature mentions a class-type "
"non-type template parameter. (#GH212351)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:577
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion caused by Microsoft integer literals exceeding the "
"maximum value. (#GH212504)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:578
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when a value of a Unicode character type "
"(`char8_t`, `char16_t`, `char32_t`) was implicitly splatted to a vector of "
"the same element type, e.g. when comparing an `ext_vector_type` of "
"`char32_t` with one of its elements. (#GH202317)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:579
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when checking scalar type with excess braces. (#GH69213), "
"(#GH137845), (#GH198767), (#GH207566), (#GH106180)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:580
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when a global variable in a non-default address "
"space, such as one declared with `__seg_gs`, is mapped into an OpenMP "
"`target` region. (#GH140069)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:581
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion crash when instantiating a nested requirement with an "
"invalid constraint. (#GH213575)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:582
msgid ""
"Clang now defines the GCC-compatible predefined macro `__SIG_ATOMIC_TYPE__`. "
"(#GH213895)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:583
msgid ""
"Fixed IEEE f128 complex mul/div using the IBM f128 libcalls on powerpc. "
"(#GH216820)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:584
msgid ""
"Fixed an ICE that occurred when a structured binding pack is expanded "
"outside the lambda where it was declared. (#GH214160)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:585
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where a stray closing curley brace in an OpenMP/OpenACC pragma "
"could cause pragma parsing issues when inside of a member function. "
"(#GH214195)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:586
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where preprocessor directives following comments were not "
"correctly recognized when using -C. (#GH48361)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:587
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when declaring a member template within a local class inside "
"an OpenMP region. (#GH216052)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:588
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when an OpenMP `copyprivate` clause names a non-static data "
"member that is not private in the enclosing context, which is now diagnosed, "
"a data member inside a member function template, or a structured binding. "
"(#GH217893)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:591
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when a variable implicitly mapped by an OpenMP "
"`target` directive has a class type (such as `std::map`) whose mapper lookup "
"instantiates a class template specialization. (#GH154704)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:593
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where repeated #imports of modular headers in non-modular "
"compilation were translated to #pragma clang module import. (#GH216924)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:594
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when `#pragma omp declare simd` or `#pragma omp declare "
"variant` is followed by another OpenMP declarative directive containing a "
"qualified identifier. (#GH217204)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:595
msgid ""
"Fixed crashes on an OpenMP `target` region inside a lambda or block at "
"namespace scope, including when the region used a global reference. "
"(#GH223397)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:596
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when an `asm` label names the register for a global variable "
"of incomplete type. (#GH219746)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:597
msgid ""
"Fixed an ICE hat occurred when using `__imag int/float` as lvalue in "
"assignment. (#GH119498)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:598
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure in `-Wsign-compare` when a negated or "
"complemented vector of unsigned integers was compared against a signed "
"constant. (#GH203575)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:599
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when a constant statement expression that "
"declares a variable is used as a bound of an OpenMP loop. A statement "
"expression in a bound of a non-rectangular loop is now diagnosed. (#GH153987)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:600
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where a bit-field accessed as the result of a statement "
"expression (e.g. `({ s.b; })`) was not subject to integer promotion, unlike "
"an ordinary bit-field access. (#GH221542)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:603
msgid ""
"No longer crashing due to follow-on diagnostics when there is an invalid "
"operand in a logical operator involving a vector operand. (#GH227588)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:604
msgid ""
"Fixed assertion failures caused by stale linkage information when an extern "
"variable or function declaration is merged with a preceding static "
"declaration. (#GH204759, #GH204754)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:605
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash due to typo correction mishandling custom keywords "
"`_virtual_inheritance` and `_multiple_inheritance` in `-fms-compatibility` "
"mode. (#GH228003)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:607
msgid "Bug Fixes to Compiler Builtins"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:609
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when classifying a call to a builtin with dependent arguments, "
"such as when the call is used as an `auto` non-type template argument."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:611
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when diagnosing a constant evaluation failure "
"inside a member function call synthesized by ``__builtin_invoke``. "
"(#GH185241)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:613
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in ``__builtin_dump_struct`` when ``-Werror`` promotes format "
"warnings to errors. (#GH211943)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:615
msgid ""
"Fixed wrong code generation in `__builtin_clear_padding` wherein the wrong "
"bits of the following types were cleared: `_BitInt`, struct bitfields, and "
"packed boolean vectors. (#GH215809), (#GH216063), (#GH224033)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:618
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when `__builtin_vectorelements` is applied to a "
"reference to a vector type; `vec_step` (in C++ for OpenCL) and "
"`__builtin_ptrauth_type_discriminator` similarly no longer accept reference "
"types that their evaluation silently mishandled. (#GH216997)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:622
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when constant-evaluating `__builtin_align_up`, "
"`__builtin_align_down`, or `__builtin_is_aligned` with pointers without an "
"underlying object. Null pointers  are handled as aligned values, while other "
"base-less pointers are rejected during constant evaluation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:627
msgid "Bug Fixes to Attribute Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:629
msgid ""
"Fixed crash (assertion) when the `alloc_align` attribute was applied to a "
"declaration whose type has a `FunctionProtoType` but which is not itself a "
"`FunctionDecl`, such as a function-pointer variable. (#GH122058)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:631
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on `bool` vectors declared with `ext_vector_type` and more "
"than 2^23 elements; `ext_vector_type` and `vector_size` now both reject "
"vectors with more than 2^23 elements or larger than 2^28 bytes. (#GH165458)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:635
msgid ""
"The `counted_by`/`counted_by_or_null` diagnostic that rejects a pointer "
"whose pointee is a struct with a flexible array member (e.g. ``struct "
"with_fam * __sized_by(size) ptr;``) was incorrectly also applied to the "
"`sized_by`/`sized_by_or_null` attributes. Because `sized_by` and "
"`sized_by_or_null` describe the size in bytes rather than a count of "
"elements, they are now correctly accepted on such pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:642
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when an `address_space` attribute with a dependent argument "
"was written after the declarator-id, where it appertains to the declared "
"entity rather than to a declarator chunk. (#GH196982, #GH111463)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:646
msgid "Bug Fixes to C++ Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:648
msgid ""
"Fixed lambdas with specifiers or attributes after the capture list being "
"misparsed as function declarations in direct-initialization contexts under `-"
"fms-extensions` or in HLSL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:652
msgid ""
"Fixed the destruction timing of temporaries created by default member "
"initializers during aggregate initialization. Such an initializer is part of "
"the full-expression containing the aggregate initialization. (#GH85601)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:656
msgid ""
"Fixed false-positive module ODR diagnostics when a type is found through a "
"using-declaration in one definition and directly in another. ODR hashing "
"also now distinguishes differently qualified uses of types found through "
"using-declarations. (#GH78850)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:660
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when diagnosing module ODR violations for enum underlying "
"types found through using-declarations with the same name but different "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:663
msgid ""
"Fixed a false type mismatch when a typedef naming an anonymous enumeration "
"was used through a C++20 named module and its defining header was "
"subsequently included. (#GH213299)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:667
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where `__typeof__` incorrectly rejected cv-qualified function "
"types."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:669
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when `#embed` was used in the braced initializer "
"of an array new-expression, or of an array whose elements are of class type. "
"(#GH128985)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:673
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where top-level CV qualifiers (such as ``const``) were dropped "
"from pointers modified by Microsoft pointer attributes (like ``__ptr32`` and "
"``__ptr64``) and WebAssembly's ``__funcref``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:675
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where we accepted ``__super`` being qualified by a scope "
"specifier, causing codegen to assertion fail elsewhere. (#GH212988)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:676
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when typo correction replaced or dropped the qualifier of "
"a name such as `foo::S<int>` while the parser was deciding whether a "
"parenthesized construct like `(void(foo::S<int>))` is a type-id or an "
"expression. (#GH221890)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:680
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where we tried to compare invalid NTTPs for variable "
"declarations, which ended up in hitting an assertion with a constrained non-"
"plain-auto NTTP, which we don't quite implement yet. (#GH208658)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:682
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a using-declaration naming an unresolvable member of a "
"dependent base was shadowed by an invalid using-declaration. (#GH209427)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:685
msgid "Fixed a CTAD bug when combining with concepts. (#GH124715)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:687
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where an internal-linkage function (e.g. a `static` or "
"anonymous-namespace helper) declared in the global module fragment of the "
"current translation unit was removed from the overload set when the calling "
"template was instantiated after the global module fragment was closed, "
"producing a spurious \"no matching function\" error with no candidate notes. "
"(#GH210822)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:694
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when module directive export module foo not following a "
"semicolon and there are no rest pp-tokens in current module file. (#GH187771)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:697
msgid ""
"Fixed concept evaluation bugs where some declarations were not added to the "
"current instantiation scope. (#GH198052)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:700
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a lambda parameter pack was given a default argument that "
"is a pack expansion referencing an enclosing function's parameter pack (e.g. "
"`[](Types... = args...) {}`). Clang now diagnoses the illegal default "
"argument instead of asserting. (#GH210714)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:705
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash on invalid code where a ``decltype`` not followed by ``(`` was "
"parsed where a nested-name-specifier could appear (e.g. ``int decltype = 0;"
"``). Clang now diagnoses the error instead of asserting. (#GH211207)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:709
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when a parenthesized structured binding "
"declarator was followed by a function declarator and body (e.g. ``([a, b])() "
"{}``). (#GH218144, #GH193687)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:713
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when computing the implicit deletion of a defaulted comparison "
"operator required an access check that ran while an enclosing declaration "
"was still being parsed. (#GH210692)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:717
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when a call to a class object was resolved through a "
"conversion function to a function pointer that was introduced into the class "
"by a using-declaration (e.g. `using Base::operator auto;`). Such a "
"conversion function is now also diagnosed if it is deleted. (#GH189146)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:722
msgid ""
"A workaround that was introduced to fix an issue with the `<format>` header "
"present in some versions of libstdc++15 has been extended to support "
"preprocessed input. Previously, splitting the preprocessing and compilation "
"step would result in the fix not being applied. (#GH160314)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:726
msgid ""
"A defaulted copy or move assignment operator for a union was left with an "
"empty body and copied nothing when the operator was actually called, for "
"example through a pointer to member. Clang now synthesizes a whole-object "
"copy so the union's object representation is copied, matching the defaulted "
"union copy constructor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:732
msgid ""
"Compute value dependence correctly for structured bindings. This mostly "
"affect C++26 constexpr structured bindings and expansion statements, but "
"also affects some uses of plain structured bindings. (#GH211930)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:736
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when instantiating the body of a C++26 expansion "
"statement after a fatal error had occurred. (#GH214917)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:739
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when an invalid statement appeared in a ``switch`` "
"statement nested inside a C++26 expansion statement. (#GH210575)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:742
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when a ``matrix_type`` with constant dimensions and a "
"dependent element type was instantiated with an invalid element type. "
"(#GH202744)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:746
msgid ""
"Fixed friend declarations sometimes making non-visible default arguments "
"incorrectly visible to default argument redefinition checks across modules."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:749
msgid ""
"Fixed handling of SFINAE failures for expressions which depend on in-class "
"member initializers of templates which are not yet parsed. An example is "
"using ``__is_constructible`` on a nested class template inside the "
"definition of the containing class. (#GH215166)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:754
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash issue when a value dependent recovery init appeared in "
"constant evaluation context in default constant evaluator."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:757
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where Clang incorrectly required `promise.return_value()` for a "
"dependent `co_return` operand that inits to `void`, instead of using "
"`promise.return_void()`. (#GH218368)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:761
msgid ""
"Fixed merging of lambdas across modules in the case where neither lambda is "
"imported from an AST file. (#GH214560)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:764
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a non-type template parameter of reference type is bound "
"to a subobject and is used in a context that requires an implicit "
"conversion. (#GH215900)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:768
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when mangling an abbreviated function template whose "
"return type has an ABI tag. (#GH204178)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:771
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion during template argument deduction where a function "
"parameter pack is referenced by other types in the function type. "
"(#GH28877), (#GH213760)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:773
msgid ""
"Fixed a regression where deprecation warnings were omitted for synthesized "
"deduction guide. (#GH160543)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:776
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when a redeclaration of a function template or an out-of-"
"line definition of a member of a class template added a default argument to "
"a parameter that follows a parameter pack (e.g. `template <typename... T> S::"
"S(T..., int = 10) {}`).  (#GH216211)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:780
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when instantiating a late-parsed function "
"template defined in an earlier translation unit with -fdelayed-template-"
"parsing. (#GH217073)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:782
msgid ""
"Allow redeclaration lookup to consider conversion function templates, "
"allowing Clang to match an in-class specialization such as `template<> "
"operator int()` against a prior conversion function template `template<class "
"T> operator T()`. (#GH218261)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:787
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when an ill-formed qualified member function definition "
"inside a union caused the union to be treated as a polymorphic class. "
"(#GH213854)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:791
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash, a miscompile and a rejected-valid case when instantiating a "
"constructor whose mem-initializer used parenthesized aggregate "
"initialization, e.g. ``: agg({1, 2})`` or ``: arr(1, 2)``. (#GH176161, "
"#GH189005, #GH213284)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:795
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when a type-trait keyword that had already been made "
"available as an identifier (e.g. `struct __make_unsigned`) was seen again in "
"a token that was lexed and cached before the first occurrence was parsed. "
"(#GH214128)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:799
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when a coroutine keyword appeared inside a mem-initializer on "
"a function that is not a constructor. (#GH194298)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:802
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when a defaulted comparison operator was synthesized for "
"a class with an invalid non-static data member, such as one qualified with "
"an address space. (#GH194605)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:806
msgid ""
"Fixed deduction of the template parameters appearing in the type of a "
"constant template parameter of reference type. (#GH40328)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:809
msgid ""
"Fixed an issue where an explicit specialization of a constexpr variable "
"would result in a link error. (#GH219796)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:812
msgid ""
"Fixed ambiguous overload where two non-static member functions with "
"different signatures could be incorrectly considered equivalent. (#GH224499)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:815
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when explicitly instantiating a nested member "
"with  an ill-formed template argument. Clang now checks for a failed "
"declaration  lookup before asserting that the name is not dependent, "
"avoiding an assertion  after an earlier diagnostic has caused the "
"declaration to be unavailable. (#GH220525)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:820
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in constant evaluation when a new-expression selects a user-"
"declared allocation function that takes std::nothrow_t by value. Such a new-"
"expression is now correctly rejected in a constant expression because it "
"does not select a replaceable global allocation function. (#GH212211)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:825
msgid ""
"Fixed `__attribute__((used))` and `-fkeep-inline-functions` being "
"incorrectly ignored for complete constructors and destructors (C1/D1 "
"variants) when `-mconstructor-aliases` is active. C1/D1 variants were "
"previously replaced with their base variants (C2/D2) in the IR before "
"retention could take effect, causing them to be dropped from llvm.used and "
"omitted from the object file. (#GH226572)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:832
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when the initializer of a variable template "
"specialization with a deduced type is instantiated from inside a lambda in "
"the initializer of another specialization of the same variable template. "
"(#GH134148)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:837
msgid "Bug Fixes to AST Handling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:839
msgid ""
"Fixed a non-deterministic ordering of unused local typedefs that made "
"serialized PCH/AST files and `-Wunused-local-typedef` diagnostics non-"
"reproducible across runs. (#GH209639)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:843
msgid ""
"`FunctionDecl::getReturnTypeSourceRange()` now returns correct source "
"location of a trailing return type. (#GH162649)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:846
msgid ""
"Added missed information to the AST node representing the member function "
"when calling a explicit object member function. (#GH218829)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:849
msgid "Miscellaneous Bug Fixes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:851
msgid "Miscellaneous Clang Crashes Fixed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:853
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in CTAD for type alias templates when the aggregate deduction "
"guide could not be resolved. (#GH206994)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:854
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when instantiating an invalid dependent friend destructor "
"declaration in a class template. (#GH210234)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:855
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure in `-extract-api` when a documentation comment "
"contains invalid UTF-8. (#GH212393)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:857
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash in codegen on 32-bit targets caused by a struct too large to "
"represent in `size_t`. The `err_struct_too_large` check now scales the "
"threshold to the target's `size_t` width instead of using a fixed threshold "
"of `1 << 60` regardless of the target."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:861
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when generating fake uses for parameters of bodyless "
"destructors with `-fextend-variable-liveness`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:862
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when filling in the ``TypeLoc`` for an ``AttributedType`` that "
"was inherited from a different declarator, for example when ``__typeof__`` "
"resolves to the type of another, already-processed declaration. (#GH217489)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:866
msgid ""
"Fixed a crash when the constant evaluator default-constructed or copied a "
"very large array, such as a local ``T s[0xFFFFFFFF][0]`` of an empty class "
"``T``. Such evaluations now fail once the element count exceeds the ``-"
"fconstexpr-steps`` limit, as they already did for ``new``. (#GH173728)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:870
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when instantiating a block that captures `this` "
"via a member access through a dependent base class."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:872
msgid ""
"Fixed `DiagnoseUnguardedAvailability::TraverseIfStmt` dereferencing a "
"nullptr on `if consteval {}`. (#GH220004)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:874
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion when the `dim` argument to an OpenACC `gang` clause "
"evaluated to a value not representable by a signed integer, such as an "
"unsigned wrap around. (#GH221418)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:877
msgid ""
"Fixed an assertion failure when a method or function definition follows an "
"Objective-C `@implementation` that was ended by a nested `@interface`, "
"`@protocol` or `@implementation` before its `@end`. (#GH209503)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:880
msgid ""
"Fixed use-after-free with annotate attribute on a C++ class method with a "
"this-adjusting thunk."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:882
msgid "OpenACC Specific Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:884
msgid "OpenCL Specific Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:886
msgid ""
"Extensions ``cl_khr_extended_bit_ops``, ``cl_khr_integer_dot_product``, "
"``cl_khr_subgroup_extended_types``, ``cl_khr_subgroup_rotate``, "
"``cl_khr_subgroup_shuffle``, and ``cl_khr_subgroup_shuffle_relative`` are "
"promoted to core features in OpenCL C 3.1. A target claiming OpenCL C 3.1 "
"conformance without supporting one of these features is now diagnosed."
msgstr ""

