msgid "NVPTX Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:911
msgid "X86 Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:913
msgid "Support `AVX10_V2_AUX` ISA (`-mavx10v2aux`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:915
msgid "Arm and AArch64 Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:917
msgid ""
"Added support for pointer authentication discrimination of C++ virtual table "
"pointers stored in VTTs via the `-fptrauth-vtt-vtable-pointer-"
"discrimination` option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:921
msgid "Android Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:923
msgid "Enabled PAC and BTI by default for AArch64 Android targets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:925
msgid "Windows Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:927
msgid ""
"Clang now accepts ``_except`` as an alias for ``__except`` in SEH handler "
"position when ``-fms-compatibility`` is enabled, matching the existing "
"``_try``, ``_finally``, and ``_leave`` aliases. ``_except`` remains an "
"ordinary identifier outside that context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:932
msgid ""
"Fixed ``setjmp`` on 32-bit Arm passing the frame pointer, rather than the "
"stack pointer as it was on entry to the function, as the frame value the CRT "
"stores in the ``jmp_buf``. Clang now uses ``llvm.sponentry`` there, as it "
"already did on AArch64."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:937
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where Clang did not match the MSVC ABI on Arm64 when an over-"
"aligned base class is followed by another base class. MSVC on Arm64 (but not "
"Arm64EC or x64) reuses the tail padding of the over-aligned base for the "
"subsequent base; Clang now does the same. ([#210174](https://github.com/llvm/"
"llvm-project/issues/210174))"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:943
msgid "LoongArch Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:945
msgid ""
"`loongarch32-*-none-elf` and `loongarch64-*-none-elf` targets now use the "
"bare-metal toolchain, like other bare-metal targets. The linker is run "
"directly instead of through `gcc`, and host include directories are no "
"longer searched."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:950
msgid "RISC-V Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:952
msgid ""
"Fixed a bug where the `interrupt` attribute did not accept `machine` "
"together with both `SiFive-CLIC-preemptible` and `SiFive-CLIC-stack-swap`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:955
msgid ""
"Added a new warning when the same interrupt type is specified more than once "
"in a RISC-V `interrupt` attribute."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:958
msgid "SiFive CLIC preemptible interrupt handlers now support frame pointers."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:960
msgid ""
"Added `-march=native` for better compatibility with ARM, AArch64, and X86. "
"This option will be treated like `-mcpu=native` if `-mcpu` is not present. "
"If `-mcpu` is present, the ISA will be selected from the host CPU and the "
"tune CPU will be selected from `-mcpu`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:965
msgid "CUDA/HIP Language Changes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:967
msgid ""
"HIP compilations now add the `include/libhipcxx` directory from the selected "
"ROCm installation to the header search path when it exists. This allows "
"libhipcxx headers to be included with paths such as `<cuda/std/atomic>`. The "
"`-nogpuinc` option disables this path together with the other HIP include "
"paths."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:973
msgid "CUDA Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:975
msgid ""
"Added `--cuda-emit-nvcc-abi` to emit the NVCC-compatible host registration "
"ABI (`__cudaRegisterLinkedBinary`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:978
msgid ""
"Fixed CUDA built-in variables such as `threadIdx` and `blockDim` being "
"incorrectly treated as having side effects in assumptions. (#GH181340)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:980
msgid ""
"Clang now provides device-side definitions of `__cxa_pure_virtual()` and "
"`__cxa_deleted_virtual()`; previously, any (potential) call to a pure/"
"deleted virtual function that could not be optimised out would cause the "
"program to fail to assemble. This is now fixed. (#GH49183) (#GH67533)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:985
msgid "AIX Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:987
msgid "NetBSD Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:989
msgid "WebAssembly Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:991
msgid ""
"Added `__builtin_wasm_memory_copy` and `__builtin_wasm_memory_fill` builtins "
"for the WebAssembly `memory.copy` and `memory.fill` bulk memory instructions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ReleaseNotes.md:994
msgid ""
"Fixed a \"function signature mismatch\" trap at program exit when destroying "
"a temporary that is bound to a reference with static or thread storage "
"duration. (#GH45221)"
msgstr ""

